#4471 combines different problems. Its one-fix summary and subject-only deduplication are not reliable guides to the actual cause. The table counts unique report IDs merged into #4471 in the 4 October export. The desk continues to receive and merge reports, so this is a snapshot, not a live count.

<Incident4471Split />

## Month/day parser

The shared parser reads month first even for day-first tenants. Dates such as 7 April can become 4 July. Fix parsing using the tenant's date order and add ambiguous-date tests. The five reports the desk read as one-day moves remain counted here, as the export's classification specifies.

## Booking form hint

The booking-v3 form tells people to enter MM/DD/YYYY even when their tenant uses day-first dates, while the form reads their entry in tenant order. Correct the hint to match the format accepted by the form and test both day-first and month-first tenants. This is not the shared parser defect.

## Reports read as one-day moves

Five reports listed in `desk-notes.json` were read by the desk as one-day moves. The export's classification counts them where filed and footnotes the different reading; they remain in the parser count. Their symptoms merit follow-up, but the export does not establish a separate cause.

## Triage

Deduplicate on demonstrated cause and affected path, not subject or intake tag alone. Confirm unclear reports against the reporter and revisit counts as the desk works. The existing accepted decision record remains unchanged; replace it with a new decision if the desk adopts a new rule.

